    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **26 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe customerCode format change was isolated to a single function class, `AssignCustomerCode.java`.\n\n**What changed** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`):\n- Old format: `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a **global** sequence (`findAll().size() + 1`).\n- New format: `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 CITY3 is the upper-cased first three letters of the city, LAST3 the first three of the last name, and NNNN a **per-city** 4-digit sequence computed by counting existing owners in that same city and adding one. The step still runs before `save`, so the new owner isn't counted in its own sequence.\n\n**Derived values rebuilt automatically:** The `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is derived as `<customerCode>-M<YY>` straight from `getCustomerCode()`, so it picks up the new city-prefixed code with no change needed \u2014 confirmed by Cp14. No other value derives from customerCode (membershipTier keys off namesake count/email; householdId is independent).\n\n**Verification:** The three spec tests pass (Cp16 format regex `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`, Cp09 per-city consecutive sequence for two Sydney owners, Cp14 membership number over the new code), and the entire suite of 26 tests remains green.",
